# Citation metadata — GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this file.
# preferred-citation is the bioRxiv preprint; update on journal publication.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use mE-DIA, please cite both the software and the paper below."
title: "mE-DIA: multi-enzyme DIA proteomics pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Plug-and-play multi-enzyme data-independent acquisition workflow that maximises
  proteome sequence coverage by splitting a sample across multiple proteases,
  recombining the digests, and co-analysing them in a single DIA-MS injection.
  Library generation is fully in silico; no DDA runs are required.
type: software
